# Bridge Units/Stream — commands, exit codes, wall times (2026-11-21)

Working directory for all Lean runs: `code/tests/lean`
(`$env:PATH="$env:USERPROFILE/.elan/bin;$env:PATH"`).
Lean 4.35.0 (x86_64-w64-mingw32), core libraries only.

| # | command | exit | wall |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `lake build Metronome.Machine Metronome.Units Metronome.Stream` | 0 | (cached oleans already present) |
| 2 | `lake env lean Metronome/Bridge/Units.lean` | 0 | 7.8 s |
| 3 | `lake env lean Metronome/Bridge/Stream.lean` | 0 | 5 s |
| 4 | `lake env lean -o .lake/build/lib/lean/Metronome/Bridge/Units.olean Metronome/Bridge/Units.lean` | 0 | 13.4 s (both files, incl. olean write) |
| 5 | `lake env lean -o .lake/build/lib/lean/Metronome/Bridge/Stream.olean Metronome/Bridge/Stream.lean` | 0 | (same run as 4) |
| 6 | `lake env lean build/lean_scratch_bridge_us/Axioms.lean` | 0 | 3.0 s |

Notes

* Both bridge files are *not* imported by `Metronome.lean` (that file is owned by
  another workstream and was not edited), so `lake build` does not build them.
  They are checked directly with `lake env lean`, and step 4 writes their oleans
  into `.lake/build/lib/lean/Metronome/Bridge/` so that the `#print axioms` file
  (step 6) can import them.
* Step 2 and step 4 report warnings only: `if_pos`/`if_neg`/`if_true`/`if_false`
  are deprecated names for `ite_eq_left`/`ite_eq_right`/`ite_true`/`ite_false`.
  No error, no `sorry`.
* The scratch directory `build/lean_scratch_bridge_us/` is temporary and deleted
  after the run.
* `git diff --quiet HEAD -- src` was run after the proofs: no output, so `src/`
  is untouched.

